  "structure": "Ten 6 EC courses each in the first two years, then 30 EC elective study, three 6 EC courses and a 12 EC individual thesis. The main chart and course record agree on 12 EC. The specialisation subtable misprints 6 EC. The 2026–2027 course guide allows students who complete the named Applied Econometrics minor to replace QRM III with another programme course. The displayed route uses the prescribed QRM III. SAM is uncredited.",
  "progression": "The adopted 2026–2027 annual schedule and course catalogue establish 60 EC per year for the Economics track. The main chart and thesis course record support 12 EC for the individual thesis despite an inconsistent specialisation subtable. The BSA threshold is 42 first-year EC including the QRM I quality requirement. SAM is uncredited mentoring. The English diagnostic or completed refresher gates the Academic Skills grade. The second-year Research Paper is a three-student theoretical or empirical project with a paper, referee report and presentations. QRM I and II and Academic Skills are recommended. Thesis application requires 120 EC including QRM II, all first-year courses and at most two remaining second-year courses. It includes a literature review or empirical or theoretical analysis and a video pitch. Minor entry normally requires 90 EC. Elective study has level, non-overlap and approval conditions. The Economics and Business Administration university minors are unavailable to Economics and Business Economics students.",
